  <content>
  <section><title>Determine the Strength of a Linear Relationship</title>
<para>Finding a Correlation Coefficient</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="1" type="enumerated">
  <item>Calculate the correlation coefficient for cricket-chirp data in the table below.</item>
  <item>Tell if the linear relationship is positive or negative and if it is strong, weak, or moderate.</item>
</list>
<table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
  <thead>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Chirps</entry>
      <entry>44</entry>
      <entry>35</entry>
      <entry>20.4</entry>
      <entry>33</entry>
      <entry>31</entry>
      <entry>35</entry>
      <entry>18.5</entry>
      <entry>37</entry>
      <entry>26</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Temperature</entry>
      <entry>80.5</entry>
      <entry>70.5</entry>
      <entry>57</entry>
      <entry>66</entry>
      <entry>68</entry>
      <entry>72</entry>
      <entry>52</entry>
      <entry>73.5</entry>
      <entry>53</entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="1" type="enumerated">
  <item> Using graphing technology, enter the chirps in the \(x\)-column of the table and the temperature in the \(y\)-column of the table. The correlation coefficient is \(r=0.9509\). </item>
  <item>This value is very close to 1, which suggests a strong, positive, linear relationship.</item>
</list>
<title>Try It: Determine the Strength of a Linear Relationship</title>
<para>Calculate the correlation coefficient for data in the table below. Tell if the linear relationship is positive or negative and if it is strong, weak, or moderate.</para>
<table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
  <thead>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(x\)</entry>
      <entry>21</entry>
      <entry>25</entry>
      <entry>30</entry>
      <entry>31</entry>
      <entry>40</entry>
      <entry>50</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(y\)</entry>
      <entry>17</entry>
      <entry>11</entry>
      <entry>2</entry>
      <entry>-1</entry>
      <entry>-18</entry>
      <entry>-40</entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

<example><exercise>
  <problem> 
    
  <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(r=-0.9985\), The relationship is a strong and negative linear relationship. </para>
</solution></exercise>
</example></section>
</content>
